Transaction Control Language (TCL):-
It is a set of SQL commands used to control and manage transactions in the database.

COMMANDS :- 1. COMMIT ,  2. ROLLBACK  ,  3. SAVEPOINT

1. COMMIT:-
It is used to save the changes permanently in the database.
SYNTAX:-COMMIT;

2. ROLLBACK:-
It is used to undo the changes that are not saved permanently.
SYNTAX:-ROLLBACK;

3. SAVEPOINT:-
It is used to create a temporary point inside a transaction.
SYNTAX:-SAVEPOINT savepoint_name;
